#
# Milestone M9 of the OCaml reference engine: 3 conformance case(s).
#
# Tab stops, widows and indentation.
#
# One case identifier per line, in the order `jlreq-conformance list` prints
# them. A `#` line and a blank line are comments. The nine files partition the
# eighty-nine built-in cases: every case is in exactly one of them, so the
# cumulative suite M1..Mn grows monotonically and M1..M9 is the whole suite.
#
# M9 is complete when the cumulative suite through M9 runs green:
#
#   cat engines/ocaml/milestones/M{1..9}.ids | ...select from suite.ndjson...
#   cargo run -p jlreq-conformance -- run ENGINE PARTIAL.ndjson   # exit 0

3.6.2/specified-character-tab-is-direction-independent
3.6.3/exhausted-stop-continues-at-next-line-first-stop
3.5.4/widow-keeps-two-clusters-on-last-line
